            "review_title": "Review at Con Ga Trong Garden",
            "review_text": "Mashajo\nKaliningrad, Russia11765 contributions\n18\nCambodian cuisine in Ho Chi Minh City\nJul 2025 • Solo\nWent into this place because it was right next to the hotel where I was staying. And frankly, a lucky coincidence - inside is very beautiful. Lots of sets, statuettes, different themed installations, all of which create an atmosphere you want to immerse yourself in. There are several rooms, many tables, enough space. Employees are friendly, speak English, help with choices. Asian cuisine is on the menu, but the emphasis is still on Cambodian dishes. Prices are just above average. I ordered spring rolls and duck breast. It was almost impossible to wait - everything was brought in quickly and simultaneously. The serving is beautiful, the portions generous. They are delicious: the duck was particularly pleased - juicy meat and a very successful sauce that perfectly complements the dish. The service is attentive and polite, the waiters are always in plain sight, but not imposed. All in all, it's a nice place to go for dinner.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten December 2, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
